\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Eternal light! Eternal light!
\par How pure the soul must be,
\par When, placed within Thy searching sight,
\par It shrinks not, but, with calm delight,
\par Can live, and look on Thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The spirits that surrounds Thy throne
\par May bear the burning bliss;
\par But that is surely theirs alone,
\par Since they've never, never known
\par A fallen world like this.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O how shall I, whose native sphere
\par Is dark, whose mind is dim,
\par Before the ineffable appear,
\par And on my naked spirit bear
\par The uncreated beam?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. There is a way for man to rise
\par To that sublime abode:
\par An offering and a sacrifice,
\par A Holy Spirit's energies,
\par An advocate with God-
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. These, these prepare us for the sight
\par Of holiness above:
\par The sons of ignorance and night
\par May dwell in the eternal Light,
\par Through the eternal Love!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

